## Why This Is Asked
Tests a beginner's grasp of Conditional Access basics and practical gating for real-world apps.

## Key Concepts
- Conditional Access
- Location and device-based access
- Intune device compliance
- Sandbox validation and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Illustrative CA policy snippet (formatting for clarity)
{
  "applications": {"include": ["https://contoso-app" ]},
  "conditions": {
    "locations": {"include": ["trusted"]},
    "devices": {"include": ["compliant"]},
    "users": {"include": ["AllUsers"]}
  },
  "grant": {"operator": "OR", "builtInControls": ["mfa"]}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this policy using a sandbox user and what logs would you inspect?
- What are common pitfalls when combining location-based and device-based CA policies?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests pragmatic cross-tenant least-privilege control and auditability for short-term access to a data workspace, combining PIM, Entitlement Management, Conditional Access, and cloud-native logs.

## Key Concepts

- Azure AD PIM: time-bound privileged access
- Azure AD entitlement management and B2B guest provisioning
- Conditional Access: MFA and device/compliance requirements
- Databricks workspace RBAC/Unity Catalog scoping
- Cross-tenant auditing: Azure AD Sign-ins, Databricks audit logs

